      "text": "To find the inverse of \\(\\mathbf{A}^2\\), we first need to determine the inverse of \\(\\mathbf{A}\\) and then use the property that \\((\\mathbf{A}^2)^{-1} = (\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2\\).\n\nGiven that \\(\\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we can find \\(\\mathbf{A}^2\\) by multiplying \\(\\mathbf{A}^{-1}\\) by itself:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^2 = \\mathbf{A}^{-1} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^{-1}\n\\]\nLet \\(\\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}\\). Then,\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^2 = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe perform the matrix multiplication:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^2_{11} = 2 \\cdot 2 + 5 \\cdot (-1) = 4 - 5 = -1\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^2_{12} = 2 \\cdot 5 + 5 \\cdot (-3) = 10 - 15 = -5\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^2_{21} = (-1) \\cdot 2 + (-3) \\cdot (-1) = -2 + 3 = 1\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^2_{22} = (-1) \\cdot 5 + (-3) \\cdot (-3) = -5 + 9 = 4\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^2 = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSince we need \\((\\mathbf{A}^2)^{-1} = (\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2\\), we calculate \\((\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2\\):\n\\[\n(\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2 = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nPerform the matrix multiplication:\n\\[\n(\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2_{11} = 2 \\cdot 2 + 5 \\cdot (-1) = 4 - 5 = -1\n\\]\n\\[\n(\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2_{12} = 2 \\cdot 5 + 5 \\cdot (-3) = 10 - 15 = -5\n\\]\n\\[\n(\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2_{21} = (-1) \\cdot 2 + (-3) \\cdot (-1) = -2 + 3 = 1\n\\]\n\\[\n(\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2_{22} = (-1) \\cdot 5 + (-3) \\cdot (-3) = -5 + 9 = 4\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n(\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2 = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe verify that:\n\\[\n(\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2 \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nPerform the matrix multiplication:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} (-1) \\cdot 2 + (-5) \\cdot (-1) & (-1) \\cdot 5 + (-5) \\cdot (-3) \\\\ (1) \\cdot 2 + 4 \\cdot (-1) & (1) \\cdot 5 + 4 \\cdot (-3) \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\begin{pmatrix} -2 + 5 & -5 + 15 \\\\ 2 - 4 & 5 - 12 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 10 \\\\ -2 & -7 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]\nis indeed the inverse of \\(\\mathbf{A}^2\\).",
