      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We first calculate $\\mathbf{A}^2.$ It can be seen that:\n$$\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\cdot 2 + 5 \\cdot (-1) & 2 \\cdot 5 + 5 \\cdot (-3) \\\\ -1 \\cdot 2 + (-3) \\cdot (-1) & -1 \\cdot 5 + (-3) \\cdot (-3) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix},$$\nso we see that $\\mathbf{A}^2 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}.$\nIt is easy to see that we will obtain the inverse of $\\mathbf{A}^2$ using the formula for finding the inverse of a $2 \\times 2$ matrix:\n$$\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}^{-1} = \\frac{1}{1 \\cdot 4 - (-1)(-5)} \\begin{pmatrix} 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -1 & \\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4} \\end{pmatrix}}.$$The answer is: \\begin{pmatrix}-1&5\\4&-1\\end{pmatrix}",
